abstract:
We report the result for a search for the leptonic decay of $B^{+} 	o \mu^{+} 
u_{\mu}$ using the full Belle data set of 711 fb$^{-1}$ of integrated luminosity collected at the $\Upsilon(4S)$ resonance with the Belle detector at the KEKB asymmetric-energy $e^{+}e^{-}$ collider. We use a fully inclusive tagging method to reconstruct the second $B$ meson and observe an excess of events. We obtain an observed branching fraction of $\mathcal{B}(B^{+} 	o \mu^{+} 
u_{\mu}) = (5.3 \pm 2.0 \pm 0.9) 	imes 10^{-7}$, corresponding to a significance of 2.4 standard deviations. We set upper limits of $\mathcal{B}(B^{+} 	o \mu^{+} 
u_{\mu}) < 8.6 	imes 10^{-7}$ (Frequentist) and $< 8.9 	imes 10^{-7}$ (Bayesian) at 90% CL.
